 a final-fight hostile after fight.over, a knocked-out or restrained person where they lie (a hit kills them: a takedown kill's consequences plus the gunfire's), a response unit or robot by its own id and a camera (\"camera:<id>\", `health.camera`; shot out it is dark for the mission; gunfire only: no hit or down Trail, no Standing) are all targets; a person shot down outside the final fight lies dead where they fell (a brief-013 body); the cell's own agents are the one target refusal (fire-on-cell). An order whose shot would fail the mission (Vale; the driver while Vale is out) always takes the `costs.loudHold` hold. Brief 030 (Sky 2026-10-20): `close`: a fire order on a target out of the weapon's reach, or with no clear line, walks the grid (at a walk) to the nearest free point inside its effective reach with a clear line (within 60 m of walk; none: refused out-of-range or no-clear-line), stands there and fires; it holds while it walks (no lapse), and a driven agent is not walked (the host drives; the order holds). `autoHolster`: a weapon drawn by a fire order or by panic (not by a draw order) is holstered by the engine `autoHolster` seconds after the fight it was drawn for ends (fight.public: quiet after its last shot, the final fight at fight.over), unless the agent still has a fire order, a stance order was given since the draw, or a hostile combatant up within its weapon's max reach has a clear line to the agent (then at the first tick none has); a weapon drawn with a draw order stays drawn until holstered.",
