e intent values and the press are confirmed (no longer proposed, no number changes); no new host field; the rulebook moves every inputs hash. 0.19.0: weapons free and hostile intent per agent (Motive tuning.md §14 with Sky's §14 note; Pulse briefs/027/pulse/hostile-initiative.md with Sky's answers 2026-10-21; both presets; rulebook weapons.free, ai.intent): weapons free is a logged cell input ({do: free, op: cell, on}; Start.weaponsFree, else weapons.free.start on; refusal free-not-cell); in a fight a drawn agent at return or free with no fire order, trigger or follow picks its attacker, else the nearest combatant in its max ring on a line, and keeps it (fire.free); precedence fire order (lock, focus), trigger, follow, weapons free, and under weapons free in a fight follow takes only a non-combatant target; cease stands an agent down until shot at (Gun.StandDown); a fight is on from a shot by or at the cell while a combatant aims at an operative in its max ring on a line, and off weapons.free.settle (line-lapse-s 3 s) after the last contact or shot (fire.free-on, fire.free-off); a focus (fire with focus: true) is a lock that never walks in (fire.focus); before the final fight a hostile fires on an agent only for that agent's seen act or own known face (ai.intent: police drawn, fired, vale, violence, the face from Alert 2; robots the same, the face at any Alert at wanted or infamous Heat; rivals calm drawn or vale, alerted also what they saw it do), never for another agent's acts or the Alert alone; a face is known when security saw the draw or violence, warned the agent, or a witness's report of violence or a draw landed; police warn a drawn weapon with no target at Alert 0-1 before any shot (the lab's warning, its numbers: 2 s, Alert 1, +1 T heeded, one a watcher); from Alert 3 at security level 1 and up police close in on a sighting by fight.kite's close-in; the guard and the patrol engage a known face they see; the rival crew watches the street from its arrival (its cone and the host's shape) and, drawn, presses for the Vale holder (KiteDisp.Press); host reads UnderFireOf (who, since, last, aiming), StandDownOf, FreeFightOn, FreeFightSince, KnownFaces, RivalsSawAct, RivalsStreetWatching, FireState mode weapons-free; faces, rivalsSaw, today's warnings, the fight's ticks and a stand-down are hashed only when set; the rulebook moves every inputs hash. 0.18.0: Motive tuning.md §13 (both presets): the count is the pair's in today too (§13.1, closing the tap-switch reset in the §11 trigger: taking a target resumes the count the shooter left on it, a target not yet fired at starts at acc.start; Gun.Mem in today, hashed only where the state does not already say it: not the target in hand at its count, not a target shot down); a holding agent never follows and is never locked by a press (§13.2); the lab's stances are three (fight.lab.stances, §13.4: a lab draw sets return); the rulebook moves every inputs hash. 0.17.0: the trigger, locks and follow fire (Sky on firing 2026-10-21, brief 024; Motive tuning.md §11; both presets; rulebook weapons.trigger, weapons.follow, follow-m 8): a logged trigger input for the driven agent (op, on, target, tick; refusal not-driven) fires on cadence while pressed and one shot per press at the first ready tick (a buffer of one), lost on a change of target, the target gone, or no reach or line when ready; a release keeps the target, the aim and the count (no tap reset); a press ends the agent's fire order, a fire order, cease, holster, the agent down or control ending ends the trigger; while it has a trigger target the driven agent's stance does not fire; a lock is a lasting fire order (engaged while its target is up); drawn agents within follow-m of the driven agent, not locked, not returning fire, not busy, carrying, inside or in the car, follow its target from where they stand (never walked, never drawn), paying aimNew: follow setting off (Start.followLock, the follow order, op cell) while the trigger is held, the aim kept on release; on, a press or a change of target locks each follower with reach and line (a fire order with its walk-in spent; fire.lock); Gun.Trig, TrigTap, TrigForce, TrigT, FollowBy and Game.FollowLock hashed only when set; host reads FollowersOf, LockOf, FireStateOf (mode, target, firing, hollow, shot, next shot, cadence, lead), FollowRingCm; the rulebook moves every inputs hash. 0.16.0: the settle and cars (Sky 2026-10-21, approved directions; Motive tuning.md §10.2, §10.7; both presets): a shooter whose run ends (a click run, or a driven run that moved) waits aimNew before its next shot, keeping its target, order and count (weapons.settle; Op.RanLast, hashed only on a run ended since the last fight tick); cars are targets ("car:getaway", "car:official", "car:rivals"; rulebook car.target: health, disabledAt, burn, blast.m, blast.damage, ×healthScale in the lab but burn and the ring): disabled at disabledAt (stops, occupants out; the getaway car fails getaway-lost), burning at 0, exploding burn s later (everyone in the ring with a line takes the blast, the cell included; people it hits cost the cell hit and down Trail, operatives none; seen by a civilian, Alert 3 and a Menace step once a car; its cover points go); a car shot is a shooting with no hit or down Trail and no Standing; GoingLoud.Fails getaway-lost, and vale-dead for the official car with Vale at it; Game.CarAt, CarOf, CarDisabled, CarBurning, CoverStanding; the range has layout lane (90 m, F8-BREAK); the rulebook moves every inputs hash. 0.15.0: fire on the move and anyone can be shot (Sky 2026-10-21; Motive tuning.md §8, §9; both presets): a fire order stops a walker and never a runner, a driven agent keeps its drive, a move given while a fire order stands keeps it and spends its walk-in (Op.CloseSpent; the order lapses weapons.lineLapse after the move ends out of reach); stances fire on the move; a shot reads the shooter's gait (walk mod.moving, run mod.running, a run away within weapons.runAwayCone mod.runningAway; the lab −1, −runPips floor 0, 0 pips = pip0), a running target past point blank takes mod.targetRunning in cover's place, and inside point blank cover counts only with weapons.pointBlankCover (false: Sky 2026-10-21, as the lab); hostiles fire as they walk in today (ai.cover.stepFires true; false is §8.3's fallback, not adopted); fire-running and fight-over are no longer given (a fire order given in the final fight still ends at fight.over; one given after it is taken and traced); a knocked-out body is a target and a hit kills; a person shot down outside the final fight lies dead (a brief-013 body, act How "shot", landed with the shooting); cameras are targets ("camera:<id>", weapons.health.camera 1; dark when shot out); GoingLoud.Fails and Hold: a shot that would fail the mission always takes the hold; FirePreview.Gait, TargetRunning, HasEnd, EndAt, AccEnd, PipsEnd, ShotsToDownEnd; the rulebook moves every inputs hash. 0.14.1: tuning.md §7.11.1: rule 4 is the blocker only (the lab's contest officer answers as any police body does); lab-only behaviour, today's hashes unchanged apart from the inputs hash (rule text). 0.14.0: police in cover answer fire (Motive tuning.md §7.10, both presets): shot at within weapons.lineLapse by an operative they see, police (officers, the response unit, police units; not robots, the guard or the patrol) fire back to their max ring; shielded and shot from beyond it they hold at most fight.kite.coverHold (3 s), then close to the shielding cover nearest their stop point (again each 3 s while shots land); the blocker and the lab's car holders answer by the max ring only; the rulebook moves every inputs hash. 0.13.0: the kite response and the 16 m sidearm in today (Sky 2026-10-20, tuning.md §7.9; rulebook fight.kite, pistol-max-m 16): armed hostiles shot at from beyond their reach answer as the lab's fight.lab.kite does (the R2 budget, the R3 police units, the no-cover close-in, the N7 re-plan), hash